  "text": "Cursor Connects to Blender and Runs Flawlessly\n\nStar_Knight12 · x · 2026-07-12\n\nThe author connected Cursor to Blender via MCP on their first try and was surprised that it \"just worked.\"\n\nThe key takeaway isn't about Blender itself, but a clear practical signal: AI coding tools are beginning to form actionable workflow connections with 3D and desktop software. For those building agent integrations, this plug-and-play experience indicates that MCP and tool-calling chains are becoming highly viable in real-world applications.\n\nRelated event: Beginner Runs Blender Rendering via Cursor and MCP(9 posts)→\n\nOriginal post →\n\nMore from coding & agent\n\nOctopus OS: a 45k-line Rust kernel where agents rewrite their own harness mid-task — _AustinCalvert_ · 2026-10-25\n\nDev argues Rust would be better if modules, not crates, were the compilation unit — zetalyrae · 2026-10-25\n\nDev open-sources BizAgent framework where one AI lead agent manages a dozen AI employees — Low-Start2333 · 2026-10-25\n\nFormal Verification Yields to Static Analysis, Which Yields to Better Language Design — xennygrimmato_ · 2026-10-25\n\nScanning 115,798 agent ledger rows: zero capability revocations, none with expiry — Affectionate-Sun265 · 2026-10-25\n\n'Slurm's defense remains annoyingly strong': dev watches agents hit HPC wall — sloppenheimer · 2026-10-25\n\ncoding & agent channel →",
